                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "67085855-ffb7-3635-805b-9e923dc59d30",
                                        "entry_id": "a6b73e9f-bb2a-3b32-84f0-5337c012b2b0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An isomorphism of a symplectic manifold; a diffeomorphism which preserves symplectic structure."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6a549b91-f50a-4e3f-bdf5-394147eaaa99",
                                                "sense_id": "67085855-ffb7-3635-805b-9e923dc59d30",
                                                "text": "In prequantizing symplectomorphisms of the type T^*g, the only special property which we used was the fact that they preserve canonical 1-forms."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6b61c1b-4616-46ac-be4e-597d3a4fe4d0",
                                                "sense_id": "67085855-ffb7-3635-805b-9e923dc59d30",
                                                "text": "Poincare's argument is based on the fact that the fixed points of a symplectomorphism of the annulus are precisely the critical points of the function #92;textstyleF(x,y)#61;#92;int#123;(fdv-gdu)#125;, where u#61;(X#43;x)#47;2, v#61;(Y#43;y)#47;2, true under the assumption that the Jacobian #92;partial(u,v)#47;#92;partial(x,y) is different from zero."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "817b5af9-608b-4f93-8c0e-a61ce27d25ec",
                                                "sense_id": "67085855-ffb7-3635-805b-9e923dc59d30",
                                                "text": "2008, Ana Cannas da Silva, Lectures on Symplectic Geometry, Springer, 2nd printing with corrections, page 63,\nThe symplectomorphisms of a symplectic manifold (M,ω) form the group\nSympl(M,ω)={f:M overset ≃⟶M|f^*ω=ω}."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
